%% Public Read Flow: Step-by-step when public users fetch and read blog posts
sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Public User<br/>(Browser)
    participant CF as CloudFront
    participant S3Blog as S3<br/>(Blog Site)
    participant S3Media as S3<br/>(Images)
    participant API as API Gateway
    participant Lambda as Lambda/<br/>EC2
    participant Prisma as Prisma<br/>ORM
    participant RDS as RDS<br/>PostgreSQL

    User->>CF: 1. GET /
    CF->>S3Blog: Cache miss → fetch site
    S3Blog-->>CF: HTML, CSS, JS
    CF-->>User: 2. Blog homepage cached

    User->>User: 3. Click "Learning AWS"
    User->>CF: 4. GET /api/posts/learning-aws-architecture

    alt Cache Hit
        CF-->>User: 5a. Cached response (5 min TTL)
    else Cache Miss
        CF->>API: 5b. Route to API Gateway
        API->>Lambda: Request post
        Lambda->>Prisma: Query post by slug
        Prisma->>RDS: SELECT posts + JOIN authors, categories, tags WHERE slug=...
        RDS-->>Prisma: Post data + relations
        Prisma-->>Lambda: Nested object
        Lambda->>Lambda: Build response (S3 image URL)
        Lambda-->>API: 6. JSON response
        API->>CF: 7. Add cache headers (max-age=300)
        CF-->>User: 8. Response cached + sent to browser
    end

    User->>User: 9. Render post HTML
    User->>CF: 10. GET /blog/123/featured.jpg

    alt Image Cached
        CF-->>User: 11a. Image from CloudFront cache (1 day TTL)
    else Image Miss
        CF->>S3Media: 11b. Fetch from S3
        S3Media-->>CF: Image data
        CF-->>User: 12. Image served + cached
    end

    User->>User: 13. Read post with featured image
